message: "Please cite the preprint and the archived repository release."
title: "A Fixed-Backbone Exclusion for Length-70 Binary (9,1) Covering Sequences"
type: software
abstract: "A reproducible fixed-backbone theorem for binary (9,1) covering sequences. For an explicit 64-edge support, every connected nonnegative integral circulation of total mass 70 has overlap at most 61, and a complete classification proves that none of the eight connected overlap-61 completions is a radius-1 cover. Therefore every valid length-70 cover has overlap at most 60 with this backbone. The result does not construct or exclude a length-70 covering sequence and does not change the known bounds on L(9,1)."
